    "quickSummary": "Under the IRS 1099 Safe Harbor Rule, independent contractors owe $0 underpayment penalty if they pay either 90% of their current year tax liability or 100% of their prior year total tax (110% if prior year AGI exceeded $150,000) across four quarterly Form 1040-ES installments. Self-employment tax is 15.3% calculated on 92.35% of Schedule C net profit, making 25% to 30% of net profit the ideal reserve benchmark.",
